        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T00:14:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I assume that using `std::vector` here is okay?  In the bug I noted that I may have seen a different Skia API for doing this, but I can\u0027t remember right now what it was... (and it is quite possible that I am misremembering...).",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 208,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 208,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "9462c01701c55c934255e1a6d9f843923a79d760",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7515e03e_5552526f",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 208,
      "author": {
        "id": 5631
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T18:40:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Skia has `SkAutoMalloc`, but `std::unique_ptr\u003cuint8_t[]\u003e` would be fine, too.",
      "parentUuid": "6621765f_98a4952b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 208,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 208,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "9462c01701c55c934255e1a6d9f843923a79d760",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "f7b5ad49_d6a7f5d5",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 12
      },
      "lineNbr": 208,
      "author": {
        "id": 8704
      },
      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T20:24:41Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Skia has `SkAutoMalloc`, but `std::unique_ptr\u003cuint8_t[]\u003e` would be fine, too.\n\nThanks for pointing out those APIs.\n\nI find it interesting that Chromium now frowns upon `std::unique_ptr\u003cuint8_t[]\u003e` (a specific instance of a more generic problem where pointers and sizes are kept/passed separately).  See also https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/main/docs/unsafe_buffers.md#Heap_allocated-arrays\n\nI note that `std::vector` had 2 properties that may have been a bit desirable: 1) initializing the memory to `0x00` was done as part of the constructor call and 2) it was convertible to `SkSpan`, and 3) it avoided the need for `reinterpret_cast`.  We could fix 2 and 3 if we added a `uint8_t* data()` and `size()` accessors to `SkAutoMalloc`.  OTOH, I am not sure if working with `SkSpan::subspan` is better or worse than using `srcRow +\u003d srcRowSize`.  In theory `SkSpan::subspan` can perform runtime bounds checks, but maybe using `SkSpan` is non-idiomatic in Skia + maybe there are performance concerns around those checks.\n\nDone?\n\nDo you think I should also add `uint8_t* data` and `size` accessors to `SkAutoMalloc` in this CL?",
      "parentUuid": "7515e03e_5552526f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 208,
        "startChar": 4,
        "endLine": 208,
        "endChar": 15
      },
      "revId": "9462c01701c55c934255e1a6d9f843923a79d760",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7f44fa08_59d225a9",
        "filename": "experimental/rust_png/impl/SkPngRustCodec.cpp",
