      "writtenOn": "2024-08-13T21:47:07Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e I assume that it is okay if `MakeFromStream` may fail (returning `kIncompleteInput`) if the input stream doesn\u0027t yet cover `IHDR` chunk.  IIUC the GIF decoder follows the same behavior.\n\n👍\n\n\u003e \n\u003e In practice `MakeStream` needs to build a color profile and therefore it may need to decode everything until the first `IDAT` chunk.  I assume that this is also okay - there doesn\u0027t seem to be a way around this (since `SkCodec` takes `SkEncodedInfo` as a parameter and `SkEncodedInfo` needs to take into account `gAMA`, `iCCP`, etc.).\n\n👍\n\nYes, the idea is that you don\u0027t need an `SkCodec` if we couldn\u0027t find all the header type information.",
      "parentUuid": "57723242_69320153",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 27,
        "startChar": 93,
        "endLine": 27,
        "endChar": 94
